  "fields": {
    "title": "Creative Coding",
    "textContent": {
      "data": {},
      "content": [
        {
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": "Description",
              "nodeType": "text"
            }
          ],
          "nodeType": "heading-3"
        },
        {
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": "Creative Coding refers to a process of exploration, iteration and reflection that uses code as the primary medium or tool to create artwork. In this way, creative coders engage in creative dialogue with the computer through the use of a programming language. ",
              "nodeType": "text"
            }
          ],
          "nodeType": "paragraph"
        },
        {
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": "Creative Coding and generative design are often treated as synonymous, but they actually refer to different practices. While creative coding is linked to a computer as a tool, generative design is a method that is independent of technology and has been used for centuries in architecture, art and graphic design. The focus here is on the development of autonomous systems, rules or algorithms that serve the basis for the creation of media in the broadest sense. Representatives of this style or working method include Karl Gerstner, Gottfried Jäger, Manfred Mohr and Karl Martin Holzhäuser. Creative Coding, on the other hand, refers to a process based on the playful discovery and exploration of the possibilities of code, without pursuing a predefined goal.",
              "nodeType": "text"
            },
            {
              "data": {
                "target": {
                  "sys": {
                    "id": "2H1Col2vuFpl58MGBSiKfZ",
                    "type": "Link",
                    "linkType": "Entry"
                  }
                }
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "data": {},
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "superscript"
                    }
                  ],
                  "value": "[1]",
                  "nodeType": "text"
                }
              ],
              "nodeType": "entry-hyperlink"
            },
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": "",
              "nodeType": "text"
            }
          ],
          "nodeType": "paragraph"
        },
        {
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": "The term Creative Coding in particular has gained popularity in recent years. It is frequently associated with ",
              "nodeType": "text"
            },
            {
              "data": {
                "target": {
                  "sys": {
                    "id": "6JvYGsB3Z0POfT9EnP867B",
                    "type": "Link",
                    "linkType": "Entry"
                  }
                }
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "data": {},
                  "marks": [],
                  "value": "frameworks",
                  "nodeType": "text"
                }
              ],
              "nodeType": "entry-hyperlink"
            },
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": " such as ",
              "nodeType": "text"
            },
            {
              "data": {
                "uri": "https://processing.org/"
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "data": {},
                  "marks": [],
                  "value": "processing",
                  "nodeType": "text"
                }
              ],
              "nodeType": "hyperlink"
            },
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": " or ",
              "nodeType": "text"
            },
            {
              "data": {
                "uri": "https://p5js.org/"
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "data": {},
                  "marks": [],
                  "value": "p5.js",
                  "nodeType": "text"
                }
              ],
              "nodeType": "hyperlink"
            },
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": ", which are particularly popular among designers and artists due to their beginner-friendly environment. Not only the use of these frameworks, but also a certain aesthetic that looks deliberately computer-generated is often associated with Creative Coding, even though Creative Coding is not limited to specific frameworks or aesthetics.",
              "nodeType": "text"
            }
          ],
          "nodeType": "paragraph"
        },
        {
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": "Background",
              "nodeType": "text"
            }
          ],
          "nodeType": "heading-3"
        },
        {
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": "The use of code to create visual art is a practice that has its origins in the 1960s. With the introduction of the home computer in the 1980s, the ",
              "nodeType": "text"
            },
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "italic"
                }
              ],
              "value": "demoscene",
              "nodeType": "text"
            },
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": " developed, which became known for cracking computer games but also for developing so-called ",
              "nodeType": "text"
            },
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "italic"
                }
              ],
              "value": "demos",
              "nodeType": "text"
            },
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": ". Demos are technically highly complex visual creations, mostly real-time animations with sound, that were created with the help of code.",
              "nodeType": "text"
            }
          ],
          "nodeType": "paragraph"
        }
      ],
      "nodeType": "document"
    },
